-- title:
--   Regular stalk with Drinfeld basis and Hasse parameter, all primes
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell\mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of level $q\ell$, with $\zeta$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, $\xi$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity and $\zeta=\xi^{\ell}$. Let $H_1\le(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times}$ be the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times}\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^{\times}$, with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^{\times}$, so $H_1$ consists of the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell$. Let $K$ be the $L$-subfield of $L((\mathsf q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) of $X_{H_1}$ of level $q^2M'$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, with uniformiser $\varpi$, and with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$; let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Let $z$ be a point of the scheme [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the rings of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, respectively $A[j^{-1}]$, and assume that the germ at $z$ of $\varpi$, pulled back along the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$, lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk. Let $y$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the finite chart mapping to $z$, and assume that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), that is, every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$. Then there exist: a local Noetherian ring $R_0$, complete for its maximal ideal, with finite residue field of characteristic $q$; a complete discrete valuation ring $W_1$ with a ring homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W_1$ such that $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma\varpi)$ and $(\sigma\varpi)^{q-1}=\varepsilon_1 q$ for a unit $\varepsilon_1$, together with a local homomorphism $\iota_1:W_1\to R_0$; a ring isomorphism $\beta$ from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $R_0$; a commutative formal group $F$ over $R_0$ and $x_0,x_1\in R_0$ such that $F$ has a Drinfeld basis of level $q$ at $(x_0,x_1)$ for the maximal ideal, i.e. the $q$-th iterate series `F.nthSeries q` is a unit times the Drinfeld divisor `F.drinfeldDivisor q x₀ x₁`, with $\mathfrak m_{R_0}=(x_0,x_1)$; elements $T,w\in R_0$ with $w$ a unit and $\operatorname{coeff}_q(F.\mathrm{nthSeries}\,q)-wT\in(q)$; the facts that [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18), the $q$-expansion of the $j$-series with exponents scaled by $q$, lies in $K$ and in the finite chart algebra; an element $a_0\in W_1$, an integer $k\ge 1$, a unit $w'\in R_0$, and a monic $P\in W_1[X]$ of degree $k$ with $P.\mathrm{coeff}\,i\in\mathfrak m_{W_1}^{\,(k-i)q(q-1)/(q+1)+1}$ for all $i<k$ (natural division); such that $R_0$ is a regular local ring of Krull dimension $2$, the map $\beta$ carries the completed germ of each constant $a\in A$ to $\iota_1(\sigma a)$, and $$\beta\bigl(\text{germ at }z\text{ of }j(\mathsf q^{q})\bigr)-\iota_1 a_0=w'\cdot(P^{\iota_1})(T).$$
--
--   This is the Katz–Mazur description of the local structure of the moduli of elliptic curves with Drinfeld level structure at a supersingular point, in the form needed here: the completed local ring of the two-chart integral model of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$ at a supersingular point of the fibre over $q$ is a two-dimensional complete regular local ring carrying a formal group with Drinfeld basis and Hasse parameter $T$, and the $q$-expansion coordinate $j(\mathsf q^{q})$ differs from a constant of $W_1$ by a unit times a monic polynomial in $T$ with prescribed valuations of its lower coefficients. The auxiliary prime $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ provides the rigidifying $\Gamma_1$-condition, so that the result is available for all primes $q$, including $q=2,3$; the statement feeds the construction of the Drinfeld chart and residue-field description at such a point.
